# Video Editor Development Rules

## Project Context
- **Tech Stack**: Electron + Vite + React + TypeScript + FFmpeg
- **Platform**: macOS (primary), Windows (secondary)
- **App**: ollo - Desktop video editor MVP
- **Focus**: Video import, timeline editing, trimming, export

## Core Architecture Principles

### Electron Main Process (TypeScript)
- All file system operations go through IPC handlers
- FFmpeg integration for video processing
- Secure with contextIsolation enabled
- Background processing for heavy operations

### React Frontend (TypeScript)
- Functional components with hooks
- useState/useContext for state management
- HTML5 video element for playback
- Custom timeline UI components

### Video Processing
- Use ffmpeg-static npm package (bundles FFmpeg binary)
- Extract metadata with FFmpeg
- Generate thumbnails from first frame
- Apply trims during export using FFmpeg -ss and -t flags

## Development Patterns

### File Handling
```typescript
// Store file paths (not contents) in React state
const [library, setLibrary] = useState<VideoClip[]>([]);

// Video playback via file:// protocol URLs
const videoSrc = `file://${filePath}`;
```

### State Management
```typescript
interface AppState {
  library: VideoClip[];
  timeline: TimelineClip[];
  selectedClipId: string | null;
  currentPlayheadPosition: number;
  isExporting: boolean;
  exportProgress: number;
  timelineZoom: number;
  timelineScrollPosition: number;
}
```

### Electron IPC Commands
```typescript
// Preload script exposes API via contextBridge
window.electron.extractVideoMetadata(filePath: string): Promise<VideoMetadata>
window.electron.exportVideo(clips: TimelineClip[], outputPath: string): Promise<void>

// Usage in React components
async function handleImport(filePath: string) {
  const metadata = await window.electron.extractVideoMetadata(filePath);
  setLibrary(prev => [...prev, metadata]);
}
```

## Performance Requirements

All features MUST maintain these targets (see prd-v1.md for details):
- **App load time**: < 5 seconds (cold start to interactive UI)
- **Timeline UI responsiveness**: < 50ms response time for drag operations
- **Video playback**: Smooth 30fps minimum (1080p H.264 content)
- **Timeline scrolling**: Smooth 60fps with 10+ clips
- **Export performance**: < 5 minutes for 2-minute 1080p video
- **Memory usage**: < 1GB RAM with 10 clips, < 100MB variance over 15min
- **No UI blocking**: Keep main thread responsive during video operations

## Video Processing Requirements

Every feature involving video operations MUST address (see prd-v1.md for details):
- **File handling**: Support MP4 and MOV formats only
- **Metadata extraction**: Use FFmpeg to extract duration, resolution, framerate
- **Thumbnail generation**: Extract first frame as JPEG
- **Trim operations**: Store trim data as {startTime, endTime} per clip
- **Export pipeline**: Use FFmpeg for concatenation and re-encoding
- **Auto-save**: Save project state every 30 seconds to local file system

## Testing Requirements

Follow manual testing protocol from prd-v1.md:
- **Manual validation** (mandatory): Test with real video files
- **Performance verification** (mandatory): Verify targets from prd-v1.md
- **Cross-platform testing** (mandatory): Test on macOS and Windows
- **Demo script**: 20-minute validation protocol from prd-v1.md

## Code Quality Standards

### TypeScript Requirements
- Strict type checking enabled
- Proper interfaces for all data structures
- No `any` types without justification

### React Best Practices
- Functional components with hooks
- Proper dependency arrays in useEffect
- Memoization for expensive calculations
- Error boundaries for video processing

### Error Handling
- Graceful handling of corrupted video files
- Clear error messages for unsupported formats
- Progress indicators for long operations
- Auto-save functionality every 30 seconds

## Testing Requirements

### Manual Testing Protocol
- Test with real video files (MP4, MOV)
- Verify metadata extraction works
- Test thumbnail generation
- Validate trim operations
- Confirm export produces valid MP4 files

### Performance Testing
- Timeline UI responsive with 10+ clips
- App load time < 5 seconds
- Video playback smooth 30fps minimum
- Export completes without crashes
- Memory usage < 1GB with 10 clips

### Cross-Platform Testing
- macOS (primary platform)
- Windows (secondary platform)
- File system operations work
- FFmpeg integration functions

## Common Patterns

### Video Import
```typescript
const handleFileDrop = (files: File[]) => {
  const videoFiles = files.filter(file => 
    file.type.startsWith('video/') && 
    (file.name.endsWith('.mp4') || file.name.endsWith('.mov'))
  );
  
  videoFiles.forEach(async (file) => {
    const metadata = await extractVideoMetadata(file.path);
    setLibrary(prev => [...prev, { ...metadata, id: uuid() }]);
  });
};
```

### Timeline Management
```typescript
const handleClipReorder = (dragIndex: number, hoverIndex: number) => {
  setTimeline(prev => {
    const newTimeline = [...prev];
    const draggedClip = newTimeline[dragIndex];
    newTimeline.splice(dragIndex, 1);
    newTimeline.splice(hoverIndex, 0, draggedClip);
    return newTimeline.map((clip, index) => ({ ...clip, order: index }));
  });
};
```

### Auto-Save Implementation
```typescript
useEffect(() => {
  const interval = setInterval(() => {
    if (timeline.length > 0) {
      saveProjectState({
        library,
        timeline,
        selectedClipId,
        currentPlayheadPosition,
        timelineZoom,
        timelineScrollPosition
      });
    }
  }, 30000); // Every 30 seconds

  return () => clearInterval(interval);
}, [library, timeline, selectedClipId, currentPlayheadPosition, timelineZoom, timelineScrollPosition]);
```

## Definition of Done

### Feature Complete When:
- [ ] Electron IPC handlers implemented in main process
- [ ] React components with all states
- [ ] Video processing verified with FFmpeg
- [ ] Auto-save functionality tested
- [ ] All acceptance gates pass
- [ ] Cross-platform testing done (macOS primary)
- [ ] Performance targets met
- [ ] Documentation updated

### Code Review Checklist:
- [ ] No console warnings/errors
- [ ] Proper TypeScript types
- [ ] Error handling for edge cases
- [ ] Performance considerations addressed
- [ ] Video processing operations tested
- [ ] Auto-save functionality verified
- [ ] Cross-platform compatibility confirmed